=== Quotient-lattice normalization ===
B=[1/14,13/14]^13 has side length 6/7; Q=R^13/Rn has dimension 12.
For primitive n, Lambda=pi(Z^13) and Lambda*={a in Z^13:a.n=0}.

=== Exhaustive corner checks for the width formula ===
a_l1=  2  width=12/7
a_l1=  3  width=18/7
a_l1=  6  width=36/7
a_l1= 91  width=78
a_l1=367  width=2202/7
The identity follows coordinatewise for every real box point; corners are hostile replays.

=== Flatness consequence and explicit classical bound ===
A hypothetical counterexample makes pi(B) a full-dimensional Lambda-free zonotope.
Khinchin flatness therefore selects primitive 0!=a in Lambda* with
  (6/7)||a||_1 <= Flt(12), hence ||a||_1 <= (7/6)Flt(12).
Using Flt(d)<=sqrt((d+1)(2d+1)/6)*d^(3/2):
  Flt(12)<=60*sqrt(26), so ||a||_1<=70*sqrt(26)<357.
Exact integer consequence: ||a||_1<=356.

=== Existing relation-canon comparison ===
AP {1,...,13} and {1,...,12,5460} already have (2,-1,0,...), l1=3.
THM-2144 forces a relation with l1<=3*29+10*28=367 on every zero-safe row.
The flatness cap 356 improves that total-coefficient number by 11; its geometric direction is different.
THM-2051 instead forces support 3..5 with coefficient height <=2^20: sparse but much taller.

=== Minimal-width Graver split ===
An l1-minimal relation is conformally indecomposable, hence a Graver element.
Support two gives a reduced speed ratio with numerator+denominator<=356;
there are 19314 unordered distinct coprime ratios in that atlas.
The higher branch is genuine: (1,-2,1) on speeds (3,4,5) has l1=4 and beats every pair relation.

=== Restricted-zonotope sidecar ===
pi(B) has 13 segment generators in dimension 12, is centrally symmetric,
and its center class has order dividing two because 2*(1/2,...,1/2) is integral.
The useful open constant is flatness for this restricted 13-generator, two-torsion-centered class.

=== Semantic boundary ===
The relation direction alone carries no active facets, slice intercept, root, owner, or temporal word.
A recursive LRC gain needs those sidecars; neither relation existence nor small l1 proves loneliness.
CHECKS=21
